  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammed Yousuf vs The State Of Telangana And 2 Others on 23 February, 2022",
    "facts": "Secondly, the order of detention was passed after three and half months of registration of the second crime and after eight months of release of the detenu in the first crime. It is further contended that the crimes registered against the detenu are classified as affecting the public order and in order to restrain him, As rightly contended by the learned counsel for the petitioner, the bail was granted to the detenu on 18.11.2020 and for eight months, the detaining authority kept quiet.",
    "arguments": "Learned Government Pleader sought to contend that after release on bail, the detenu is involved in one more crime and the detenu is in the habit of involving in crimes, and therefore, not desirable to release him.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned Government Pleader sought to contend that after release on bail, the detenu is involved in one more crime and the detenu is in the habit of involving in crimes, and therefore, not desirable to release him.",
